build/
build-*/
*.o
*.elf
*.bin
*.hex
*.map
*.lst
compile_commands.json
.cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Verilator output. hardware/gal/*.v and *.sv are the sources; obj_dir is
# regenerated by `npm run check:sim`.
obj_dir/

# machine_tb's frame capture. It is an OUTPUT of the simulation - one run of
# `npm run check:machine` writes it - and the claims about it are in the
# testbench, not in the file. The .ppm is what the testbench emits; the .png is
# what a human looks at.
hardware/gal/verilog/screenshot.ppm
hardware/gal/verilog/screenshot.png

# Reference scans (datasheets, service manuals, schematics). Kept out of
# history: they are ~93 MB and are freely available from the vendors and from
# colorcomputerarchive.com. Each reference/ subdirectory has a README listing
# the expected files and what cites them, so a fresh clone can be refilled.
# The READMEs themselves are deliberately not covered by these patterns.
reference/**/*.pdf
reference/**/*.tiff

# Third-party binaries and source archives that this project has no right to
# redistribute (Apple ROM images, the CHM QuickDraw/MacPaint releases). Tracked
# until 2026-09-04; see reference/68k/README.md and docs/design-review.md Sys-M6.
reference/**/*.ROM
reference/**/*.rom
reference/**/*.zip

# Vendor installers. awincupl.exe.zip is Microchip's WinCUPL, which
# hardware/gal/prjbureau/extract-wincupl.sh unpacks for the ATF15xx fitters and
# the CUPL compiler. Licensed, 20 MB, and freely downloadable - not ours to
# redistribute, and reference/README.md's rule for vendor blobs applies.
awincupl.exe.zip
*wincupl*.zip
